UPDATED Q (Updated 3/20/25): What should a covered institution submit to the FDIC if it cannot certify compliance with Part 370 by the time its annual certification is due?
A: If a covered institution cannot certify compliance with Part 370, as clarified in these FAQs and other applicable guidance, it should instead:
Identify the instances that prevent the covered institution’s Part 370 capabilities from accurately calculating deposit insurance coverage as required by the Rule;

Provide a plan and timeframe, or update its previously submitted plan and timeframe, to resolve such instances;
Explain remediation challenges to the extent they exist; and
Submit its deposit insurance coverage summary report ensuring that the deposit accounts for which the Part 370 capabilities cannot calculate deposit insurance coverage are reported in accordance with section 370.10(a)(2)(v).

